---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'

const lastUpdated = 'February 19, 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Sato"
  description="Privacy Policy for Sato, aligned with GDPR and Belgian data protection law."
  ogTitle="Privacy Policy | Sato"
  ogDescription="How Sato collects, uses, and protects personal data."
  ogUrl="https://withsato.com/privacy"
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="relative overflow-hidden bg-background pb-20 pt-36 sm:pt-44">
    <div
      class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0"
      style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 0%, hsl(220 70% 45% / 0.08) 0%, transparent 62%);"
    >
    </div>

    <section class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl px-6">
      <h1
        class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl"
      >
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        This Privacy Policy explains how Sato collects, uses, and protects
        personal data for the website and product experience. It is drafted with
        the General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and Belgian
        privacy law in mind, including the Belgian Act of July 30, 2018 on the
        protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal
        data.
      </p>
      <article
        class="mt-10 space-y-9 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground"
      >
        <section>
          <h2
            id="data-controller"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            1. Data Controller
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The data controller responsible for this processing is:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>Legal entity: Sefiani Technologies</li>
            <li>Company number (BCE/KBO): BE1015571192</li>
            <li>
              Privacy contact:
              <a
                href="mailto:privacy@asksato.ai"
                class="underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-foreground"
              >
                privacy@asksato.ai
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="scope"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            2. Scope of This Policy
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            This policy applies to personal data processed through:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>the Sato marketing website</li>
            <li>the Sato application and onboarding flow</li>
            <li>support, billing, and account operations related to Sato</li>
            <li>
              third-party integrations and messaging platforms used to interact
              with the assistant
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="personal-data"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            3. Personal Data We Process
          </h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground">Account data:</span>
              name, email, authentication identifiers, and account status.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground">Usage data:</span>
              IP addresses, browser metadata, timestamps, product events, and technical
              logs needed for security, reliability, and abuse prevention.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground"
                >Personalization preferences:</span
              >
              assistant name, communication style, use case, and additional context
              you provide during setup. This data is stored by Sato to configure your
              assistant.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground">Conversation data:</span
              >
              prompts, messages, and responses are processed on your dedicated server
              and sent directly to AI model providers. Sato does not have access to
              your conversation content.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground">Billing data:</span>
              subscription status, invoices, and payment metadata. Card details are
              handled by payment providers and are not stored by us.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground">Support data:</span>
              information you share when requesting help.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We apply data minimization and only collect data that is reasonably
            necessary to operate and secure the service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="legal-bases"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            4. Why We Process Data and Legal Bases (GDPR Art. 6)
          </h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground"
                >Contract (Art. 6(1)(b)):</span
              >
              to create your account, provide the assistant, process payments, and
              deliver support.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground"
                >Legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f)):</span
              >
              to secure the service, prevent fraud or abuse, improve reliability,
              and defend legal claims.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground"
                >Legal obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)):</span
              >
              for accounting, tax, and compliance duties under applicable law.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground"
                >Consent (Art. 6(1)(a)):</span
              >
              where legally required, such as for non-essential cookies or specific
              optional features.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="data-sharing"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            5. How We Share Data
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We do not sell personal data. We share data only when necessary
            with:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>hosting and infrastructure providers</li>
            <li>payment providers</li>
            <li>authentication providers (Google)</li>
            <li>AI/model providers acting under contractual safeguards</li>
            <li>
              messaging platforms (such as Telegram) that you connect as a chat
              interface — messages flow through their infrastructure and are
              subject to their own privacy policies. Sato does not store
              messaging platform credentials on its servers; they are only
              present on your dedicated server.
            </li>
            <li>authorities if legally required</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            All processors are subject to appropriate contractual and security
            obligations.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="international-transfers"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            6. International Transfers
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            When personal data is transferred outside the European Economic
            Area, we rely on recognized safeguards, such as adequacy decisions
            or Standard Contractual Clauses, together with supplementary
            measures where appropriate.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="data-retention"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            7. Data Retention
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We keep personal data only as long as necessary for the purposes
            above. The following guideline durations apply:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground">Account data:</span>
              retained while your account is active, plus 30 days after account deletion
              to allow for recovery and complete any pending operations.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground"
                >Billing and invoice records:</span
              >
              retained for 7 years as required by Belgian accounting law.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground">Security logs:</span>
              retained for up to 12 months, based on risk and necessity.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Actual retention may vary where required by law or legitimate
            interests. Where feasible, data is deleted, anonymized, or
            irreversibly aggregated once no longer required.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="security"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            8. Security Measures
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We implement technical and organizational safeguards appropriate to
            the risk, including access controls, encryption in transit, least
            privilege practices, and monitoring for abuse or unauthorized
            access.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            No system is perfectly secure. If a personal data breach occurs, we
            will handle it according to GDPR and applicable Belgian law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="your-rights"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            9. Your Rights Under GDPR
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Subject to legal conditions, you may request:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>access to your personal data</li>
            <li>rectification of inaccurate data</li>
            <li>erasure (right to be forgotten)</li>
            <li>restriction of processing</li>
            <li>data portability</li>
            <li>objection to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
            <li>withdrawal of consent where processing is consent-based</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To exercise your rights, contact us at
            <a
              href="mailto:privacy@asksato.ai"
              class="font-medium text-foreground underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-foreground"
            >
              privacy@asksato.ai</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="complaints"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            10. Complaints to the Belgian Supervisory Authority
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You have the right to lodge a complaint with the Belgian Data
            Protection Authority (APD/GBA):
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>
              Website:
              <a
                href="https://www.dataprotectionauthority.be"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-foreground"
              >
                www.dataprotectionauthority.be
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>Email: contact@apd-gba.be</li>
            <li>Address: Drukpersstraat 35, 1000 Brussels, Belgium</li>
            <li>Phone: +32 (0)2 274 48 00</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="cookies"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            11. Cookies and Similar Technologies
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We use necessary cookies and similar technologies to operate the
            service securely. These include:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground"
                >Session and authentication cookies:</span
              >
              essential for keeping you signed in and maintaining your session state.
              These do not require consent as they are strictly necessary for the
              service to function.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="font-medium text-foreground"
                >Non-essential cookies:</span
              >
              if we introduce analytics or similar non-essential cookies in the future,
              they will only be placed after obtaining your consent through a cookie
              banner or settings mechanism.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="automated-decisions"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            12. Automated Decision-Making
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Sato uses artificial intelligence to provide its personal assistant
            features. AI processing — including generating responses,
            suggestions, and summaries — happens on your dedicated server via
            third-party model providers, not on Sato's infrastructure. We do not
            use automated processing, including profiling, to make decisions
            that produce legal effects or similarly significant effects on you
            (GDPR Art. 22).
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You remain in control of any actions taken as a result of AI
            responses.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you have questions about how AI is used to process your data,
            contact us at
            <a
              href="mailto:privacy@asksato.ai"
              class="font-medium text-foreground underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-foreground"
            >
              privacy@asksato.ai</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="children"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            13. Children
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Sato is not intended for children. If we become aware that personal
            data has been provided in violation of applicable age requirements,
            we will take appropriate steps to delete or restrict that data.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            id="changes"
            class="scroll-mt-28 text-lg font-semibold text-foreground"
          >
            14. Changes to This Policy
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect
            legal, technical, or business changes. Material updates will be
            notified by appropriate means. The latest version is always
            published on this page.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>

      <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Last updated: {lastUpdated}
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
